_TAG_START --><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21.99 4c0-1.1-.89-2-1.99-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v12c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h14l4 4zM20 4v13.17L18.83 16H4V4zM6 12h12v2H6zm0-3h12v2H6zm0-3h12v2H6z"/></svg><!-- HTML_TAG_END --> </div> <div class="loading-dots yf-k991ov" data-svelte-h="svelte-1b7fhl7"><div class="dot yf-k991ov"></div> <div class="dot yf-k991ov"></div> <div class="dot yf-k991ov"></div> </div> </button></div> <div class="byline-comments-mobile yf-z1ictt">    <button class="icon2-btn fin-size-medium view-cmts-button    rounded   highlightWhenExpanded yf-7mptsx" data-ylk="elm:cmmt_open;elmt:cmnt;itc:1;slk:comments;sec:content-canvas;subsec:ycp" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;cmmt_open&quot;,&quot;yLinkElementType&quot;:&quot;cmnt&quot;,&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;comments&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;ySubModuleName&quot;:&quot;ycp&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas ycp&quot;}" title="Comment" aria-label="Comment"><div aria-hidden="true" class="icon fin-icon inherit-icn sz-large  yf-15ilbqr"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21.99 4c0-1.1-.89-2-1.99-2H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v12c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h14l4 4zM20 4v13.17L18.83 16H4V4zM6 12h12v2H6zm0-3h12v2H6zm0-3h12v2H6z"/></svg><!-- HTML_TAG_END --> </div>  </button></div></div> </div>   <div class="body-wrap yf-1qcy35b">  <div class="body yf-v6n2s3" data-testid="article-body">  <div class="bodyItems-wrapper">        <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Some economists might find the latest jobs numbers underwhelming, especially compared to the eye-popping results from the early post-pandemic years — but Kevin Hassett, the director of the National Economic Council, went on <em>CNBC</em> (1)'s Squawk Box on Monday (2) to argue the numbers look worse than they are because the Trump administration has cracked down on immigrants, who previously propped up payroll reports.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>    <div class="wrapper yf-2smqn1" data-testid="inarticle-ad">   <div id="sda-INARTICLE-5533a9ec-fbfc-367e-bbcf-f0a8cd0a0df3-1" class="sdaContainer  dv-all sda-INARTICLE-5533a9ec-fbfc-367e-bbcf-f0a8cd0a0df3-1 yf-d5hqm1 overflow margin  visible placeholder" data-testid="ad-container" data-ad-unit="/22888152279/us/yfin/ros/dt/us_yfin_ros_dt_mid_center" data-ad-size="970x250,728x90,970x90,300x250,fluid" data-ad-region="main-dynamic" data-ad-loc="mid_center" style="--placeholder-height: 250px;"> </div></div>        <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->"The jobs numbers right now have been blockbuster," Hassett said. "The breakeven job number is a lot lower than it used to be because we've tightened the border. And so 120,000, 130,000 this year is sort of like 200,000 two or three years ago because we don't have this massive inflow of immigrants that are working."<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <h2 class="text text-block heading text-left neo-font-heading-lg  yf-18d6y07" role="heading" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Must Read<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </h2>    <ul class="yf-1jsc1up"><li class="yf-1jsc1up">      <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Thanks to Jeff Bezos, you can now <a href="https://moneywise.com/investing/real-estate/invest-vacation-rental-homes-v?throw=DM1_yahoo&amp;placement_syn=placement_1&amp;utm_source=syn_oath_mon&amp;utm_medium=BL&amp;utm_campaign=185419&amp;utm_content=syn_31fccb8c-0d4d-4e95-acd9-4996034eea08" data-ylk="slk:become%20a%20landlord%20for%20as%20little%20as%20%24100;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;become a landlord for as little as $100&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">become a landlord for as little as $100</a> — and no, you don't have to deal with tenants or fix freezers. Here's how<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p> </li><li class="yf-1jsc1up">      <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Robert Kiyosaki says <a href="https://moneywise.com/news/investing/robert-kiyosaki-says-this-1-asset-will-surge-400-in-a-year-warns-prices-are-about-to-explode-urges-investors-not-to-miss-out-do-you-own-any?throw=DM2_yahoo&amp;placement_syn=placement_1&amp;utm_source=syn_oath_mon&amp;utm_medium=BL&amp;utm_campaign=185419&amp;utm_content=syn_19701688-7f94-458a-9b57-9fc49a8591e4" data-ylk="slk:this%201%20asset%20will%20surge%20400%25%20in%20a%20year;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;this 1 asset will surge 400% in a year&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">this 1 asset will surge 400% in a year</a> and begs investors not to miss this 'explosion'<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p> </li><li class="yf-1jsc1up">      <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Dave Ramsey warns nearly 50% of Americans are making 1 big Social Security mistake — <a href="https://moneywise.com/managing-money/retirement-planning/dave-ramsey-warns-nearly-50-of-americans-are-making-1?throw=DM3_yahoo&amp;placement_syn=placement_1&amp;utm_source=syn_oath_mon&amp;utm_medium=BL&amp;utm_campaign=185419&amp;utm_content=syn_d62684a0-920a-409e-9631-7cce05852986" data-ylk="slk:here's%20how%20to%20fix%20it%20ASAP;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;here's how to fix it ASAP&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">here's how to fix it ASAP</a><!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p> </li> </ul>        <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->The April jobs report (3) had something for both sides of the argument. Job creation topped expectations for the month, with nonfarm payrolls up by a seasonally adjusted 115,000 for April, but average hourly earnings came in lower than expected — and the month also saw a noticeable drop in the labor force and tech-related jobs.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>    <div class="wrapper yf-2smqn1" data-testid="inarticle-ad">   <div id="sda-INARTICLE-5533a9ec-fbfc-367e-bbcf-f0a8cd0a0df3-2" class="sdaContainer  dv-all sda-INARTICLE-5533a9ec-fbfc-367e-bbcf-f0a8cd0a0df3-2 yf-d5hqm1 overflow margin  visible placeholder" data-testid="ad-container" data-ad-unit="/22888152279/us/yfin/ros/dt/us_yfin_ros_dt_mid_center" data-ad-size="970x250,728x90,970x90,300x250" data-ad-region="main-dynamic" data-ad-loc="mid_center_2" style="--placeholder-height: 250px;"> </div></div>        <h4 class="text text-block heading text-left neo-font-label-2xl-emphasis  yf-18d6y07" role="heading" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->How the 'breakeven' jobs number works<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </h4>        <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Hassett's perspective on the jobs numbers is based on the breakeven, or the number of jobs the economy must add each month to keep the unemployment rate from drifting up. When immigration rises, the breakeven climbs. When it slows, the same payroll figure starts signaling a tighter labor market.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->For historical scale, a Federal Reserve staff note published last month (4) noted the breakeven averaged around 80,000 a month in the 2010s and ran as high as 185,000 in the 1970s, when baby boomers and women were flooding into the workforce.<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><strong>Read More: </strong><a href="https://moneywise.com/real-estate/real-estate/fundrise-private?throw=HALF_yahoo&amp;placement_syn=placement_2&amp;utm_source=syn_oath_mon&amp;utm_medium=BL&amp;utm_campaign=185419&amp;utm_content=syn_bb5514e7-0d8d-4af3-a0cf-4a427d254675" data-ylk="slk:This%20%241B%20private%20real%20estate%20fund%20is%20now%20accessible%20to%20non-millionaires.%20Start%20investing%20with%20just%20%2410;elm:context_link;itc:0;sec:content-canvas;source:content-canvas%20default" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;This $1B private real estate fund is now accessible to non-millionaires. Start investing with just $10&quot;,&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;context_link&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yTrafficOrigin&quot;:&quot;content-canvas default&quot;}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><strong>This $1B private real estate fund is now accessible to non-millionaires. Start investing with just $10</strong></a><!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>        <h4 class="text text-block heading text-left neo-font-label-2xl-emphasis  yf-18d6y07" role="heading" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->What economists are still debating<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </h4>         <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Some economists have offered partial support for Hassett's framing. Chicago Fed President Austan Goolsbee told (5) <em>CNBC</em> (6) on Friday the labor market has been "pretty much stable for a year, year and a half," calling it as stable "without being good." Dan North, senior economist for North America at Allianz, told <em>CNBC</em> the report was "fairly bulletproof this month."<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>  </div>  <div class="readmore  yf-11souuj">    <button class="secondary-btn fin-size-large readmore-button    rounded   highlightWhenExpanded yf-7mptsx" data-ylk="elm:readmore;itc:1;sec:content-canvas;slk:Story%20Continues" data-yga="{&quot;yLinkElement&quot;:&quot;readmore&quot;,&quot;yModuleName&quot;:&quot;content-canvas&quot;,&quot;yLinkText&quot;:&quot;Story Continues&quot;}" aria-label="Story Continues" title="Story Continues"> <span>Story Continues</span> </button> </div> <div class="read-more-wrapper" style="display: none" data-testid="read-more">   <div class="wrapper yf-2smqn1" data-testid="inarticle-ad">   <div id="sda-INARTICLE-5533a9ec-fbfc-367e-bbcf-f0a8cd0a0df3-3" class="sdaContainer  dv-all sda-INARTICLE-5533a9ec-fbfc-367e-bbcf-f0a8cd0a0df3-3 yf-d5hqm1 overflow margin  visible placeholder" data-testid="ad-container" data-ad-unit="/22888152279/us/yfin/ros/dt/us_yfin_ros_dt_mid_center" data-ad-size="970x250,728x90,970x90,300x250" data-ad-region="main-dynamic" data-ad-loc="mid_center_3" style="--placeholder-height: 250px;"> </div></div>       <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg  yf-18d6y07" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Others are not sold. Joseph Brusuelas, chief economist at RSM US, pushed back earlier this year (7) on attributing softer hiring to demographics, calling it "an attempt to distract from immigration and trade policies." Kory Kantenga, LinkedIn's head of economics for the Americas, told <em>CNN</em> (8) that "half of the job gains came from retail and transportation and warehousing; those are sectors that do not consistently add jobs."<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </p>       <h2 class="text text-block heading text-left neo-font-heading-lg  yf-18d6y07" role="heading" style="text-decoration: none; font-style: normal; text-transform: none; text-align: inherit; font-variant-numeric: normal;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->You May Also Like<!-- HTML_TAG_END -->  </h2>   <ul class="yf-1jsc1up"><li class="yf-1jsc1up">      <p class="text text-block paragraph text-left neo-font-paragraph-xl-reg