00 for April, but average hourly earnings came in lower than expected — and the month also saw a noticeable drop in the labor force and tech-related jobs.\",\"type\":\"text\",\"attrs\":{},\"hydratedAsset\":null},{\"asset\":null,\"legacyAttrs\":{\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"characterCount\":37,\"level\":4,\"id\":null},\"attribs\":null,\"nodeId\":\"27\",\"parentNodeId\":null,\"text\":null,\"type\":\"heading\",\"attrs\":{\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"characterCount\":37,\"level\":4,\"id\":null},\"hydratedAsset\":null},{\"asset\":null,\"legacyAttrs\":{},\"attribs\":null,\"nodeId\":\"28\",\"parentNodeId\":\"27\",\"text\":\"How the 'breakeven' jobs number works\",\"type\":\"text\",\"attrs\":{},\"hydratedAsset\":null},{\"asset\":null,\"legacyAttrs\":{\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"characterCount\":296},\"attribs\":null,\"nodeId\":\"29\",\"parentNodeId\":null,\"text\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"attrs\":{\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"characterCount\":296},\"hydratedAsset\":null},{\"asset\":null,\"legacyAttrs\":{},\"attribs\":null,\"nodeId\":\"30\",\"parentNodeId\":\"29\",\"text\":\"Hassett's perspective on the jobs numbers is based on the breakeven, or the number of jobs the economy must add each month to keep the unemployment rate from drifting up. When immigration rises, the breakeven climbs. When it slows, the same payroll figure starts signaling a tighter labor market.\",\"type\":\"text\",\"attrs\":{},\"hydratedAsset\":null},{\"asset\":null,\"legacyAttrs\":{\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"characterCount\":242},\"attribs\":null,\"nodeId\":\"31\",\"parentNodeId\":null,\"text\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"attrs\":{\"textAlign\":\"left\",\"characterCount\":242},\"hydratedAsset\":null},{\"asset\":null,\"legacyAttrs\":{},\"attribs\":null,\"nodeId\":\"32\",\"parentNodeId\":\"31\",\"text\":\"For historical scale, a Federal Reserve staff note published last month (4) noted the breakeven averaged around 80,000 a month in the 2010s and ran as high as 185,000 in the 1970s, when baby boomers and women wer