1. **Critical, new | Row 2, what-happened.** “Kevin Hassett, the director of the National Economic Council, is the title Yahoo Finance used on September 4.” The [pinned Yahoo page](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/coverage/yahoo-hassett-august-jobs.html:797) says `>May 11, 2026</time>` and its metadata says `"datePublished":"2026-05-11T20:55:00Z"`. The [live article](https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/articles/kevin-hassett-says-jobs-numbers-205500419.html) also dates itself May 11. The sentence gives this article a September 4 date it does not have. Yahoo carried the title in a May article about the April jobs report; the manifest’s September 4 date is wrong.

2. **Minor, residual | Row 9, where-this-sits.** “The Associated Press counted a different stretch, an average 68,000 jobs a month so far this year, against 9,700 average new jobs created every month in 2025.” The pinned [payroll series](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/PAYEMS-2026-10-03.csv:1033) gives `"2024-12-01,158316"`, `"2025-12-01,158432"` and `"2026-09-01,159044"`. Those levels yield about 9,700 per month in 2025 and 68,000 through September 2026. “The Associated Press counted” credits the outlet for figures available from the pinned primary series. This was reported in the [r1 red-team review](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-03-r1-redteam.md:3); the [later pace patch](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/working-notes/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.md:781) retained the attribution. The correct account is that AP reported averages calculable from the BLS payroll series.

3. **Minor, residual | Row 1, what-happened.** “Reuters wrote that government payrolls contracted 17,000, mostly in local government, excluding education.” The pinned BLS table gives `"| Government | 23,568 | 22,138 | 22,499 | 23,355 | 23,543 | 23,300 | 23,344 | 23,327 | -17 |"` and `"| Local government, excluding education | 6,885.4 | 7,213.0 | 7,155.6 | 6,950.0 | 6,898.4 | 6,974.4 | 6,978.9 | 6,968.3 | -10.6 |"` ([BLS pin](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/data/sources/bls-empsit-2026-09.txt:1722)). The numbers are supported, but the sentence credits Reuters for a breakdown in the pinned primary. The [r10 records review](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-05-r10-records.md:5) reported this; the [later placement patch](/Volumes/4/GitHub/the-catch-site-wt-jobs-sept/checks/working-notes/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.md:787) left the attribution. The correct account is a 17,000 government payroll decline, including 10,600 in local government excluding education.

